{{also|lǐfà|lǐfǎ}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|lifa}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*libjaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*leyp-||leave, cling, linger}} (cognate with {{cog|fo|liva}}, {{cog|sv|leva}}, Danish and Norwegian {{m|da|leve}}, {{cog|nl|leven}}, {{cog|de|leben}}, {{cog|en|live}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈlɪːva/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪːva|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lifði|lifað}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[live]]
#* Genesis 5:3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20bók%20Móse+5:3&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%205:3&version=NIV English])
#*: {{quote|is|Adam '''lifði''' hundrað og þrjátíu ár. Þá gat hann son í líking sinni, eftir sinni mynd, og nefndi hann Set.|When Adam had '''lived''' 130 years, he had a son in his own likeness, in his own image; and he named him Seth.}}
# to [[experience]] something {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{syn|is|reyna}}
# to [[survive]], to [[endure]], to [[come through]] {{+obj|is|&intransitive/acc}}
#: {{syn|is|endast|þrauka}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''lifi'''.|I'll '''come through'''.}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive|of fire}} to [[burn]]
#: {{syn|is|loga|brenna}}
#: {{ux|is|Eldurinn '''lifir'''.|The fire is '''burning'''.}}

